Subject: [PATCH] Screen, app_server: a UI scale choice (Automatic, 100%, 150%, 200%)

The UI scale is the default font size: controls, window borders, icons and
the cursor all follow it. Setting it meant changing four font sizes by hand,
and once chosen they stuck, whatever display the system booted on.

The Screen preferences get a "UI scale" menu. 100%, 150% and 200% size the
plain, bold, fixed and menu fonts to 12, 18 and 24 pt. "Automatic" sizes them
by the display's pixel density, the way app_server does when no sizes were
chosen, and leaves "auto" in ~/config/settings/system/app_server/ui_scale:
app_server then picks the scale on every start, ignoring the saved sizes.
A font size chosen by hand in Appearance shows as "Custom". The choice also
goes to ~/config/settings/rretina_resize as host_scale (1 for Automatic), so
on QEMU's virtio-gpu the screen follows the host window at that many pixels
per point - sharp on a Retina Mac. Afterwards Screen offers to restart
Tracker and Deskbar so the desktop picks the new size up at once.
The Screen window also follows a mode change it did not make (the resize
helper following a QEMU window): its resolution menu and monitor view show
the new mode, which also becomes the one Revert goes back to.

Ported from renkuos-apps/renku-retina (patch 0003), the same project as
0037-app-server-dpi-ui-scale -- see that patch for why this is baked
into the image rather than left to a later pkgman install. Applies
cleanly as-is to this port's pinned commit.

